---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use"
  description="The conditions that apply when you use Playarr software and the public playarr.app service."
>
  <Section eyebrow="Legal" title="Terms of use">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="legal-effective-date">Effective 28 August 2026</p>
      <h2>Using Playarr</h2>
      <p>
        By using Playarr or playarr.app, you agree to these terms and the <a href="/legal/acceptable-use">acceptable-use policy</a>. If you do not agree, do not use the software or hosted service.
      </p>
      <h2>Your server and media</h2>
      <p>
        Playarr supplies no media, and the maintainers operate no media service. Playarr can
        pass the requests your users make to a request manager, or to your own Radarr or Sonarr,
        that you have configured; what those applications then do is set up and controlled by the
        operator and is the operator's responsibility, and Playarr itself obtains no media. You are
        responsible for the legality of what you store, play and share, for the server you
        connect to, the accounts you create, the people you invite and compliance with the laws
        that apply to you.
      </p>
      <h2>Support</h2>
      <p>
        Maintainers may refuse support, close issues and decline contributions that fall outside
        the <a href="/legal/acceptable-use">acceptable-use policy</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Service availability</h2>
      <p>
        The public linking service is provided as a convenience and may change, be interrupted or be withdrawn. Keep direct access to your self-hosted server available; the hosted service is not a backup for your server or data.
      </p>
      <h2>No revenue, no subscription, no data sold</h2>
      <p>
        Playarr earns no revenue from you. There is no subscription and no paid tier, and no
        personal data is sold. See the <a href="/legal/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Software licence and warranty</h2>
      <p>
        Playarr's source is made available under the MIT licence described on the <a href="/legal/licences">licences page</a>. The software is provided “as is”, without warranty of any kind. In plain words, it may contain faults, it may not suit your purpose, and nobody promises that it will work or keep your data safe. To the maximum extent permitted by law, the software and hosted service are provided ‘as is’, and the developers are not liable for any claim, damage or loss, including indirect, incidental, special or consequential loss, arising from using them.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Rights holders and others reporting abuse can write to
        <a href="mailto:support@playarr.app">support@playarr.app</a>. Please include the work
        concerned, where it appears, your contact details, and a statement that you believe in good
        faith that the use is not authorised. Playarr hosts no content, so complaints about media on
        a self-hosted server go to the operator of that server.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        Material changes will be published on this page with a new effective date. Continuing to use the hosted service after a change means accepting the revised terms.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: var(--width-prose);
  }

  .prose h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
  }

  .legal-effective-date {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
</style>
